# Configurable columns, through the real window.
#
# What no unit test reaches here is the reconcile: ColumnLayoutRules decides the list, but whether
# DetailsView.Columns ends up matching it — after a search, after a clear, after a drag — is a
# property of the view. assert-visible cannot see a GridViewColumn (it is not a FrameworkElement and
# never enters the visual tree), which is why assert-column and assert-columns exist.

tree .
refresh

# The starting set is what the five fixed columns always were. Anything that changes
# ColumnCatalog.Defaults without meaning to goes red here.
assert-columns Name, Size, Type, Modified
columns

# --- The two columns the app places itself ---

# Folder follows the flattening, and is gone the moment the search is cleared. It also lands between
# the name and everything else rather than on the end.
search report
assert-flattened
assert-columns Name, RelativePath, Size, Type, Modified
clear-search
assert-no-column RelativePath

# Match follows ShowsContentMatches, not IsFlattened. An ordinary search flattens and must NOT bring
# it: mutate ColumnLayoutRules.Resolve to key it on isFlattened and the next two lines go red.
search report
assert-no-column Match
clear-search

content-fixture
refresh
search content:needle
assert-flattened
assert-column Match
assert-columns Name, RelativePath, Match, Size, Type, Modified
shot 01-match-column
clear-search
assert-no-column Match

# Neither of them is a choice, so neither survives into the saved layout — a hand-edited settings
# file naming one must not get a second copy, or one in a listing where it means nothing.
columns add RelativePath
assert-no-column RelativePath

# --- Adding, removing, reordering, resizing ---

columns add Created
assert-columns Name, Size, Type, Modified, Created
columns remove Type
assert-columns Name, Size, Modified, Created
columns move Created 1
assert-columns Name, Created, Size, Modified
columns width Created 200
columns
shot 02-custom-columns

# Name is not optional and not movable. Both rules are enforced where the drag comes back through,
# not only on load, because AllowsColumnReorder has always let the header be dragged away.
columns remove Name
assert-column Name
columns move Name 3
assert-columns Name, Created, Size, Modified

# The injected columns still slot in around a customised set.
search report
assert-columns Name, RelativePath, Created, Size, Modified
clear-search

# A sort by a column that was added at runtime, which is the whole point of the ids being strings.
sort Created
sort Created
sort Name

columns reset
assert-columns Name, Size, Type, Modified

# The layout survives the session round trip the same way the pane arrangement does.
columns add Created
columns width Created 180
session
assert-columns Name, Size, Type, Modified, Created

assert-not-launched
state

# --- Shell metadata ---
#
# A real 64x64 PNG, so System.Image.Dimensions has something true to say. The read goes through
# ShellProperties.ReadValues — the keyed path, not the enumerate-everything one the Properties
# dialog uses — and lands via the hydrator's coalescing pass rather than from a cell getter.
#
# assert-metadata reads the *rendered cell*, not the view model, and that is the whole point of it:
# the first version of this feature read and cached every value correctly while rendering a blank
# column, because the binding was never told the value had arrived. Asking the view model in C#
# looked perfect throughout.
preview-fixture
refresh
go Preview
columns add System.Image.Dimensions
assert-column System.Image.Dimensions
settle 400
assert-metadata sample.png System.Image.Dimensions 64
shot 03-metadata-column

# Sorting by a column that did not exist when the app was compiled, which is the whole reason the
# ids are strings rather than an enum.
sort System.Image.Dimensions
sort System.Image.Dimensions
sort Name

columns reset
assert-no-column System.Image.Dimensions
assert-not-launched

# --- The header strip, the sort marker, and the menu ---

# A right-click past the last column must open the *column* menu. That gap is a Role=Padding header
# the presenter builds itself, so it carries no menu of its own and used to fall through to the file
# list's — offering Cut, Delete and Properties for a click on nothing at all. Checked after a
# search and after a tile-mode round trip too, since both rebuild the header row.
assert-header-menu columns
search report
settle
assert-header-menu columns
clear-search
thumbnails 0.5
thumbnails 0
settle
assert-header-menu columns

# The sort marker follows the column being sorted by, and flips with the direction. Photographed
# rather than asserted: the glyph is a template trigger, and the way it fails is by rendering
# nothing while every property behind it is correct.
sort Size
settle
shot 04-sort-ascending FileListView
sort Size
settle
shot 05-sort-descending FileListView
sort Name

# The checklist, with ticks against the columns that are on. Photographed for the same reason: the
# themed MenuItem template drops the stock check indicator, so IsChecked can be perfect while
# nothing renders. Name is ticked and disabled — it cannot be turned off.
columns add Created
menu columns 06-column-menu

assert-not-launched
state

